## Screenshots
{% for interface in ui %}
{%- if interface == 'web' %}
> **To write:** the web app's screenshots. Start with a line that says the data is invented, such
> as "The screenshots show invented data from a demo run, not a real installation." Then a table
> with one row per page and a column each for a desktop and a phone capture: a bold page name and
> what the page shows, then each image linked to itself, such as
> `[<img src="screenshots/<page>.png" width="480" alt="<page>, desktop">](screenshots/<page>.png)`
> for the desktop and `width="160"` for the phone. Capture the desktop at a width such as 1440×900
> and the phone at a phone width, such as 390×844 CSS pixels at 2×.
> [Screenshots](../CONTRIBUTING.md#screenshots) in CONTRIBUTING.md says how to capture them, and
> the privacy check each one needs before it's committed.
{%- elif interface == 'desktop' %}
> **To write:** the desktop app's screenshots. Start with a line that says the data is invented.
> Then a table with one row per window or state: a bold name and what it shows, then the image
> linked to itself, such as
> `[<img src="screenshots/<window>.png" width="480" alt="<what it shows>">](screenshots/<window>.png)`.
> Capture each window at its default size.
> [Screenshots](../CONTRIBUTING.md#screenshots) in CONTRIBUTING.md says how to capture them, and
> the privacy check each one needs before it's committed.
{%- elif interface == 'terminal' %}
> **To write:** the terminal app's screenshots. Start with a line that says the data is invented,
> such as "Each screenshot is a screen of the demo mode, so every name and number in it is made
> up." Then a table with one row per screen: a bold name and what it shows, then the image linked
> to itself, such as
> `[<img src="screenshots/<screen>.svg" width="480" alt="<what it shows>">](screenshots/<screen>.svg)`.
> [Screenshots](../CONTRIBUTING.md#screenshots) in CONTRIBUTING.md says how to capture them, and
> the privacy check each one needs before it's committed.
{%- endif %}
